<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gordian III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">225–244</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gordian III was Roman emperor from 238 to 244, raised to the throne at thirteen after the deaths of his grandfather <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordian-i">Gordian I</a>, his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordian-ii">Gordian II</a> and the senatorial emperors Pupienus and Balbinus. Guided by his praetorian prefect Timesitheus, he disbanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legio-iii-augusta">Third Legion Augusta</a> for its part in the Gordians' fall and campaigned against the Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a>. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> in 244, perhaps killed by his own troops.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gordian-iii.jpg" alt="Gordian III" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marie-Lan Nguyen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bust_Gordianus_III_Louvre_Ma1063.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
